          "type": "reasoning",
          "text": "The change is in place. The module-level `signal` is `default_namespace.signal`, so it inherits the validation.\n\nRequirements check:\n- Non-string names → TypeError before lookup/modification: yes, `isinstance` check is first.\n- Even if namespace already contains that key: check precedes `if name not in self`, so `ns.signal(1)` raises even if `1 in ns`.\n- str subclasses accepted: `isinstance` accepts subclasses.\n- Empty string accepted: `\"\"` is a str instance.\n- Signal identity for repeated names: unchanged logic (`return self[name]`).\n- Original docstring preserved: docstring text unchanged (both method docstring and doc param on created signals — created once with `doc`, subsequent calls return existing signal).\n- Independent names / receiver dispatch: untouched.\n- Module-level `signal`: bound to `default_namespace.signal`, so validated.\n\nOne more consideration: should the module-level `signal` function itself be validated independently? Since it's literally the bound method, no. Behavior is identical.\n\nDone. Submit patch with summary and uncertainties.",
